  "worked_solution": "Any vector in  $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =3\\cdot (2{t}^{2}+{t}^{3})+(-2)\\cdot (1+3{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}+3{t}^{3}-2-6{t}^{2} \\\\  & =-2+3{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
